  "period_note": "Year-end position from ONE Bank PLC's FY2024 Annual Report, Solo basis; this is the report's OWN current-year column (i.e. not subject to the restatement described in the FY2023 note, which concerns FY2022/FY2023 closing balances only). Profit before tax was only 608.870m, but a large net deferred-tax INCOME of 670.915m (current tax expense 670.105m offset by a deferred-tax credit of 1,341.019m, explicitly labelled 'Prior year's balance restated') flipped this to a Net Profit After Tax of 1,279.785m - i.e. reported profit is dominated by a one-off deferred-tax recognition, not operating performance (Total Provision for loans/advances rose to 7,299.516m from 2,049.323m the prior year). SEPARATE FINDING: this report's 'Five Years' Financial Highlights' exhibit shows Net Profit After Taxation for FY2020/FY2021/FY2022 as 1,462m/1,047m/2,042m respectively - these do NOT match the originally-reported contemporaneous PAT for those years (1,313.022m/756.030m/1,391.852m), the Consolidated PAT for those years (1,394.706m/845.185m/1,558.631m), nor this SAME report's own internally-consistent 'Financial Highlights on Overall Activities of the Bank' (BB-format) table, which instead correctly reproduces the original 2022 PAT (1,391.852081m) in its own comparative column. This is treated as an isolated compilation error in that one exhibit (see sources.json) and is not used anywhere in this dataset; FY2020/2021/2022 PAT in this dataset use each of those years' own contemporaneous, internally-corroborated figures.",
